# Mask Shaman

**Alignments.** Any, but the spirits avoid selfish people.

Renowned for the Living Masks through which they channel their magic - Great
Fetishes grown, with the tree''s permission, from the living wood of a tree, and
dropping from it like ripe fruit when complete. Each mask is shaped from a
different kind of tree for a different purpose, and a Mask Shaman keeps many,
often with elaborate costumes of hide, feathers and bone to match. They are also
minor psionic healers who use fire and ash in their rituals.

## Lore

The largest and best-known society of Mask Shamans is the False Face Society
of the northeast, centred on the Iroquois Nation and reaching as far south as
North Carolina. It is always led by a woman, the Keeper of Masks, who guards
against abuse of the tree spirits. The ultimate mask would be one shaped from a
Millennium Tree; no mortal is known to have made one.

## Equipment the catalog cannot hold yet

Ceremonial garments and a ceremonial headdress or mask, a hat or hooded cloak,
moccasins, wood carving tools, a hand axe, 50 feet of rope, a ball of string, a
week of dried food, sewing needles, thread, a pint of rabbit-skin glue, 1D4+2
paint pigments, five brushes and five sticks of charcoal. Two S.D.C. weapons of
choice, usually a staff or war club.
', 'published', 'data-script'
